F438|THE 3-NODE SWARM IS PENALISED BY A METRIC THAT GETS HARDER PURELY BECAUSE IT HAS MORE NODES|The other half of F436, and the best explanation of the node curve this campaign has produced. THE DETAIL FAN SCALES BEAUTIFULLY: 1334s for 9 details on 1 node (148s each) against 249s for 19, 293s for 17, 588s for 8 and 571s for 21 on 3 nodes (13 to 74s each) - a 2x to 11x speedup, the fan working exactly as designed. THAT GAIN IS THEN HANDED BACK. Every confidence_retarget in every cell carries binding_signal agreement, and the tax is 821s on n3-r0, 786s on n3-r1 and 1657s on n3-r3, which is 40 to 57 percent of the 3-node prefix. THE ONE-NODE CELL PAID ZERO. WHY, and it is structural, not luck: skeleton_drafts shows the 1-node cell REQUESTED 2 drafts (worker_count 2) while the 3-node cells requested 3. Agreement then came out 88 on 2 drafts versus 50, 52 and 54 on 3. plan_agreement scores count-spread as max minus min and file overlap as MEAN PAIRWISE JACCARD, AND THE ENGINE'S OWN DOC SAYS BOTH ONLY WORSEN OR HOLD AS THE POOL GROWS. So a 3-draft set is scored lower than a 2-draft set of equal quality, ask_floor is a FIXED 85, and the run below it pays a full redraft ladder. MORE NODES MEANS MORE DRAFTS MEANS LOWER MEASURED AGREEMENT MEANS A TAX THAT CANCELS THE FAN. TWO FIXES ARE ALREADY BUILT AND BOTH ARE INERT ON THE ROUND THAT DECIDES: diverse_plan resolves FALSE in the runs, and its own comment calls the metric "the bug that makes the SEQUENTIAL retarget ladder run every time" and says ENFORCE lifts a strongly-converging draft set past the floor so the ladder is SKIPPED. best_subset_agreement exists to make a GROWING pool raise rather than lower the score, but round 1 uses it only when consensus_k is set and otherwise calls plan_agreement, and round 1 is exactly the round that decides whether to retarget at all. ⚠️ NOT YET A CLAIM THAT REMOVING THE TAX HELPS: retargeting cells scored 0.9343, 0.7147 and 0.8157 against 0.6030 and 0.6695 for the two that never retarge