F439|68 ORPHANED PROCESSES OVER FOUR DAYS, HOLDING PORTS THE REAPER WAS NOT WATCHING|Found while checking for a duplicate sweep before planning the rebuild. reap_stray_listeners runs between EVERY unit and had found none of them, correctly: it sweeps PORT_BASE to PORT_BASE plus 40, that is 8930 to 8970, calibrated on the single leak ever observed at port 8931. The apps under test pick their OWN ports. The live leaks held 18082, 19000, 18080, 18095 to 18101, 18765, 18123, 19001, 19004 to 19006, 8000, 8081, 8099, 9000, 9090, 9999 and 38081 - NOT ONE inside the range. The instrument was calibrated on one sample and has been finding nothing, correctly, forever. THIS IS NOT COSMETIC: F88 already recorded a stray port failing a whole unit with OSError Errno 48 Address already in use, and a test that imports the app while another process holds its port errors at COLLECT time, so a leaked server presents as a BUILD DEFECT and lands in the score. Several cells scored 0.00 on server_runs. WIDENING THE PORT RANGE IS THE WRONG FIX - 8000, 9000 and 9999 are exactly where a person's own dev server lives and this runs unattended on Mihai's machine - so the discriminator is the CWD, because every one of these was spawned by a worker inside a run directory and nothing of his is in there. AGE IS THE SECOND GUARD AND IT IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT BELT AND BRACES: run directories are REUSED, and four processes with cwd swarm-3node-r1 were 2 days 20 hours old while that cell had been running for 80 minutes. Same path, different run. ⚠️ MY FIRST GUARD WAS A COUNTDOWN, NOT A GUARD: a process-GROUP check leaves the live engine matching every condition - goose swarm run is spawned in its own group and its cwd IS a run directory - with nothing but the 3 hour age floor between it and SIGKILL, against cells that take 2.5 hours. Fixed to walk ppid to the root, and protect_root is a PARAMETER because a guard that can only be exercised by BEING the sweep is a guard nobody has ever checked. EXECUTED onc