F486|THE SINK DOES NOT ALWAYS OWN NOTHING - THE PLANNER SOMETIMES GIVES IT A DELIVERABLE, AND EVERY FIX I SHIPPED TODAY IS INERT WHEN IT DOES|The live 3-node cell judged integrate-verify OVER_READING with action RE_DISPATCH, deterministic, at 7.2 minutes - a full restart of the join, which is precisely what F473 measured costing 15 to 44 minutes and precisely the disaster the engine's own comment records as integrate-verify judge_killed three times, run reported FAILED though the app works. I went looking for a regression in my own judge change. IT IS NOT A REGRESSION AND THE VERDICT IS ARGUABLY CORRECT. THE PLANNER GAVE THE SINK A FILE. swarm-3node-r0's integrate-verify owns tests/test_integration.py, so owns_code is TRUE, the over-read gate arms legitimately, and the hint is accurate - it owes a file, has not written it, and has run four commands. MEASURED ACROSS SIX CELLS: baseline-n1-r0 gave the sink README.md, swarm-3node-r0 gave it tests/test_integration.py, and the other four gave it nothing. SO THE SINK OWNS A FILE ROUGHLY A THIRD OF THE TIME AND IT IS NOT PREDICTABLE. THE CONSEQUENCE IS THAT MY ENTIRE DAY'S PREMISE HOLDS ONLY SOMETIMES. Three of the fixes I shipped are gated on owned_files being EMPTY: the degrade-on-stall extension, the judge's owns-nothing Accept branch, and by extension the reasoning in F473 and F484 about the join being structurally unjudgeable. ALL THREE ARE INERT IN ANY CELL WHERE THE PLANNER HANDS THE SINK A DELIVERABLE, AND IN EXACTLY THOSE CELLS THE SINK BECOMES ELIGIBLE FOR AN OVER-READ RE-DISPATCH INSTEAD - the worst of both worlds, since that is the restart Mihai's directive was about. I DID NOT CHECK THIS BEFORE BUILDING, AND THE VARIANCE WAS VISIBLE IN THE FIRST CELL I EVER LOOKED AT: baseline-n1-r0's sink owns README.md and I read that plan four separate times today without noticing the field. THE ENGINE'S OWN COMMENT ALREADY DESCRIBED THIS EXACT FAILURE - in 3 runs the planner happened to give it README.md, and in two of those the gate armed and killed it repeatedly - and the owns_code guard was written to stop a DOC arming it. That guard works: README.md is not a code deliverable, so n1-r0's sink was safe. A TEST FILE IS A CODE DELIVERABLE, SO THIS ONE WAS NOT. ⚠️ I AM NOT SHIPPING A FIX TONIGHT ON ONE OBSERVATION. The question that decides it is whether a JOIN should ever own a deliverable at all - fan_verify_split rewrites integrate-verify into a thin join and evidently does NOT clear its files - and that is a planner-contract question I must read before touching. ⇒ L292 A PROPERTY YOU BUILT THREE FIXES ON IS A PROPERTY YOU MUST MEASURE ACROSS EVERY CELL FIRST - I TREATED OWNS-NOTHING AS THE SINK'S DEFINITION WHEN IT IS ONLY ITS USUAL STATE
F487|THE FASTEST 3-NODE CELL YET ALSO SCORED THE LOWEST - AND RE-RUNNING A CELL DESTROYS THE DATA POINT IT REPLACES|The first cell on tonight's binary landed: baseline-n3-r0 on build_sha f9b6d2bd6, QUALITY 0.6904, SPEED 101 MINUTES, device occupancy 0.7971. SPEED IS THE BEST A 3-NODE CELL HAS EVER POSTED ON A CLEAN BUILD - the two 3-node cells on 5cc600778 took 141 and 180 minutes, so this is 30 to 45 percent faster - AND OCCUPANCY 0.7971 IS THE SECOND-HIGHEST EVER RECORDED. It also completed all 22 tasks with ZERO retries, which no earlier 3-node cell managed. BUT QUALITY FELL TO 0.6904, BELOW BOTH 3-NODE CELLS ON THE PREVIOUS COMMIT (0.7151 and 0.9178) AND BARELY ABOVE THE 1-NODE MEAN OF 0.6355. THIS IS EXACTLY WHY MIHAI ASKED FOR TWO PILLARS. Reporting 101 minutes alone would have read as a breakthrough; reporting 0.6904 alone would have read as a regression; the pair says SPEED IMPROVED AND QUALITY DID NOT, and neither half is the story. goal.py refused to compare it at all - no 1-node cell exists on f9b6d2bd6 yet, so it printed no paired comparison in this commit, a lone arm proves nothing, which is the correct verdict and the one I would have been tempted to talk around. I CANNOT ATTRIBUTE EITHER MOVEMENT. n equals 1, the within-arm quality spread on the previous commit was 0.2027, and 0.6904 sits comfortably inside a distribution that wide. The cell carries degrade_on_stall, the judge Accept branch and the stream-drop hint but NOT sink_review and NOT the join-owns-nothing fix, and the zero retries could be those fixes or could be a night without a dropped socket. 🔴 AND THE SCOREBOARD SHRANK WHILE I WATCHED. The 5cc600778 group was n equals 2 versus n equals 2 an hour ago; it is now n equals 1 versus 2, because the sweep RE-RAN baseline-n3-r0 IN THE SAME DIRECTORY and OVERWROTE its result file. The 0.9178 / 180-minute cell that anchored this morning's comparison NO LONGER EXISTS ON DISK. That is a direct threat to the gradually improve half of the directive: a