g goes red, and nothing has yet. The value here is narrower: the provenance gates open on the right commit, the preconditions are genuinely being met rather than skipped, and the anti-overreach property has a real observation behind it. ⚠️ AND THE INJECTION IS NOW THE THING TO WATCH. At 73.8 minutes the replan added test-edge-cases::1 and harden-error-handling::1. F536 measured that in six of ten three-node runs the LAST task to complete is a replan-added bonus task, and F537 only refuses LATE injections — this one was early and legitimate, so it is fully entitled to become the tail. If it does, that is F536's mechanism firing in a cell where my own gate correctly declined to intervene, which is a sharper result than either finding alone. ⇒ L364 THE FIRST TIME A GATE YOU SHIPPED SAYS *YES* ON REAL DATA IS WORTH MORE THAN THE FIRST TIME IT SAYS NO - A REFUSING GATE AND A BROKEN ONE PRODUCE THE SAME SUMMARY, AND ONLY A DELIBERATE PERMIT DISTINGUISHES THEM
F559|THE OPTIMISATION I WAS ABOUT TO BUILD ALREADY EXISTS AND WORKS - AND HUNTING FOR THE REAL COST FOUND A SECOND SILENT WINDOW WORTH SIXTEEN MINUTES OF PREFIX|I set out to build digest-keyed detail reuse across a retarget discard, the fix F547 and F549 jointly specified, on the evidence that a discard costs plus 22.5 minutes of prefix. GREPPING FIRST KILLED IT. The engine already has `detail_memo`, DEFAULT ON since the golden bake, keyed on `detail_memo_key(goal, id, brief, files, findings)` — a hash of the FULL detailer input, so a hit means byte-identical LLM input — consulted inside the detail fan itself, printing how many subtasks it reused each round. AND IT IS WORKING WELL. Counting `detail_completed` per fan against the task count: baseline-n3-r3 ran fans of 9, 4 and 8 for nineteen tasks, twenty-one calls total, ONE POINT ONE ONE TIMES the work of a single fan rather than the three times a memo-less engine would pay — the middle fan collapsing from nine to four is the memo hitting hard. baseline-n3-r1: 9 then 13 for twenty tasks, 1.10x. The live frozen cell: 10, 10, 9 for twenty-two tasks, 1.32x, and its weaker reuse is exactly consistent with F549's measurement that this cell genuinely rewrote half its specs. THE MEMO ALREADY ABSORBS ALMOST ALL OF THE RE-DETAIL COST, so the fix I was about to write would have bought close to nothing. THIRD WRONG FIX CAUGHT BEFORE SHIPPING, and the second one this week caught by L355's rule to grep the engine before building. SO WHERE DOES THE TWENTY-TWO MINUTES ACTUALLY GO. Timing every phase boundary in the three retargeting cells: the detail FANS take 1.4 to 3.5 minutes each, which is noise. The redraft from discard to the next `skeleton_drafts` takes 4 to 5 minutes. AND BETWEEN `plan_convergence` AND THE FIRST `detail_completed` THERE IS A GAP OF 6.6 TO 8.2 MINUTES IN WHICH THE ENGINE EMITS NOTHING AT ALL. In the live cell it is 6.8, 6.7 and 6.6 minutes across three rounds — remarkably stable — and the first detail call